] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — Modesto"
  description="How the Modesto project handles information when you use the desktop app, visit modesto.dev, or connect coding-agent providers."
  heading="Modesto Privacy Policy"
  lede="This Privacy Policy describes how the Modesto project collects, uses, and shares personal information when you use the Modesto desktop application, visit the Modesto website, or download builds from our public GitHub releases."
  effectiveDate="2026-09-08"
  lastUpdated="2026-09-08"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="introduction">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) describes how Tanner Davidson and the Modesto project
      (“Modesto,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) collect, use, and share personal information when you use
      the Modesto desktop application for macOS, Windows, and Linux (the “App”), visit the Modesto
      marketing website at{" "}<a href="https://modesto.dev">https://modesto.dev</a> (the “Site”), or
      download release artifacts from the public repository at{" "}<a
        href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto">https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto</a
      > (together, the “Services”).
    </p>
    <p>
      Modesto is a local-first, open-source control plane for coding agents. The App is designed so
      that your projects, threads, prompts, diffs, and session history can stay on the machine you
      control. We do not operate a cloud session broker that receives your source code while an
      agent is working. This Policy explains the limited information we do process — mostly to
      publish the Site, ship desktop updates, and communicate with you — and the much larger set of
      information that stays with you or with providers you choose.
    </p>
    <p>
      By using the Site or the Services, you acknowledge the practices described in this Policy. If
      you do not agree with this Policy, please do not use the Site or the Services. This Policy
      does not govern third-party coding agents, model providers, identity providers, or
      infrastructure that you choose to connect to Modesto. Those parties process information under
      their own terms and privacy policies. See our{" "}<a href="/third-party">Third Party</a> notice
      for how those relationships work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="information">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Personal Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect personal information in different ways depending on how you use Modesto. Most App
      data never leaves your device unless you send it to a provider you configured.
    </p>

    <h3>Information that stays on your device</h3>
    <p>
      When you use the App, Modesto stores project paths, thread history, drafts, model and provider
      preferences, local settings, cached file and git metadata, and related workspace state on your
      machine. Credentials and session tokens use platform-provided protected storage where
      supported. This information is not collected by us unless you transmit it as part of a feature
      you initiate — for example, by sending a prompt to a coding-agent provider, opening a GitHub
      pull request, or asking the App to check for an update.
    </p>

    <h3>Personal information from users of the App</h3>
    <p>When you use the App, we may process the following categories of personal information:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Update and version information.</strong> The built-in updater may request release
        metadata from GitHub so the App can tell you when a new build is available. That request can
        include a public IP address, operating-system and architecture details, and the App version
        you are running. GitHub processes those requests under its own privacy policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Information you provide to us.</strong> We collect information that you choose to
        send when you open a GitHub issue, discussion, or security advisory, email or message the
        maintainer, or otherwise communicate with the project. That may include your GitHub
        username, email address, and the contents of your report.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Crash or diagnostic information you choose to share.</strong> The App is not
        designed to phone home with telemetry. If you voluntarily attach logs, screenshots, or
        traces to a support request, we process only what you send.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Personal information from users of the Site</h3>
    <p>
      When you visit the Site, our hosting and content-delivery providers may automatically log
      online identifiers and internet-activity information, including your Internet Protocol (IP)
      address, device and operating-system type, browser type and version, pages viewed, access
      times, referrers, and error details. We use this operational information to serve, secure, and
      troubleshoot the Site — not for targeted advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you download a desktop build from GitHub Releases, GitHub — not Modesto — records the
      download under its own terms. We may publish aggregate download counts on the Site.
    </p>

    <h3>Information we get from others</h3>
    <p>
      We may receive personal information from service providers that help us operate the Site and
      publish releases, such as GitHub, a website host, or a content-delivery network. We may
      combine that information with information you provide directly. We also receive whatever
      information a coding-agent provider returns to your App after you send it a request; that
      response is delivered to your device, not stored by us as a cloud archive.
    </p>

    <h3>Cookies and local storage</h3>
    <p>
      The Site may use cookies or similar technologies to operate essential features, remember
      theme or reduced-motion preferences, and understand whether pages are functioning correctly.
      The App stores connection settings, credentials, preferences, drafts, and cached thread, file,
      branch, and server metadata on your device. Information stored only on your device is not
      collected by us unless it is transmitted as part of a feature you use.
    </p>

    <h3>Device permissions</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Files and folders.</strong> The App accesses project directories you open so it can
        show files, diffs, and workspace context. It does not upload a project to us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Network.</strong> Used to talk to providers you configure, fetch updates you
        request, and reach local services you point the App at.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Notifications.</strong> Used only if you enable desktop notifications for agent
        status.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Camera, photos, or microphone.</strong> Used only if a feature you start needs them
        — for example attaching an image you select. Frames and files stay on your device unless you
        send them to a provider.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="uses">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>How We Use Your Personal Information</h2>
    <p>
      Subject to this Policy and the terms of third-party applications you connect, we may use
      personal information for the following purposes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>To publish, host, and operate the Site and public documentation;</li>
      <li>To distribute desktop builds and updater metadata through GitHub Releases;</li>
      <li>To respond to issues, security reports, feedback, and other communications you send;</li>
      <li>To monitor reliability of the Site, prevent abuse, and investigate security incidents;</li>
      <li>To comply with applicable law and enforce the terms governing the Services; and</li>
      <li>
        To understand, in aggregate, whether the Site and release channels are working — for
        example page availability or download counts — without building advertising profiles.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Training of AI models</h3>
    <p>
      We do not use your personal information, source code, prompts, or agent responses to train
      artificial-intelligence models. We do not operate a model-training pipeline on user
      workspaces. Providers you choose may train or evaluate models under their own policies; review
      those policies before you send them code or confidential material.
    </p>

    <h3>Compliance and protection</h3>
    <p>We may use personal information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Comply with applicable laws, lawful requests, and legal process;</li>
      <li>Protect the rights, privacy, safety, and property of Modesto, our users, and others;</li>
      <li>Audit our processes for legal, contractual, and policy compliance;</li>
      <li>Enforce the terms that govern the Site and the Services; and</li>
      <li>
        Prevent, identify, investigate, and deter fraudulent, harmful, unauthorized, unethical, or
        illegal activity, including abuse of the Site or release infrastructure.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>How We Share Your Personal Information</h2>
    <p>
      We may disclose the categories of personal information described above to the following
      categories of third parties.
    </p>

    <h3>Providers you choose</h3>
    <p>
      At your direction, prompts, files, screenshots, and related content are sent from your App to
      coding agents and model providers you configure — for example Codex, Claude, Cursor, Gemini,
      Grok, and other supported harnesses. Because you bring and authenticate those providers, the
      applicable third parties vary by installation. They process information under their own terms
      and privacy policies. Modesto does not sit in the middle as a cloud archive of those
      sessions.
    </p>

    <h3>Infrastructure used to publish Modesto</h3>
    <p>
      We use specialized providers to host the Site, deliver static assets, and publish desktop
      builds. Depending on how you reach Modesto, these may include:
    </p>
    <ul class="provider-list">
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub</strong> <em>(GitHub, Inc.)</em>.<br />
        We use GitHub to host the source repository, issues, discussions, security advisories, and
        release artifacts, and to serve updater metadata.<br />
        You can view GitHub’s privacy statement here:{" "}<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
          >https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Website hosting and content delivery.</strong><br />
        The Site is served by a hosting and CDN provider so pages load quickly and remain available.
        Those providers may process IP addresses and request logs as described above.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These providers process information for us under their own contractual and privacy
      obligations. We do not use an advertising network, and we do not sell personal information.
    </p>

    <h3>Professional advisors and successors</h3>
    <p>
      We may share personal information with lawyers or other professional advisors in the course of
      the services they provide to the project, and in connection with a merger, acquisition,
      reorganization, or similar transaction involving Modesto. If another party assumes
      responsibility for the project, that party may possess the personal information collected
      under this Policy and assume the rights and obligations described here.
    </p>

    <h3>Legal and safety disclosures</h3>
    <p>
      We may disclose personal information if we believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary
      to comply with law or legal process; protect or defend the rights, property, or safety of
      Modesto, users of the Site or the Services, or others; investigate or prevent fraud, abuse, or
      unlawful activity; or enforce this Policy and the terms governing the Services. We may also
      share personal information at your direction or with your consent.
    </p>

    <h3>No sale of personal information</h3>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral or targeted
      advertising.
    </p>

    <h3>Third-party websites and services</h3>
    <p>
      The Site and the App may contain links to third-party websites or services, including GitHub,
      documentation for providers, and download mirrors. When you follow a third-party link or
      connect a third-party service, that third party may collect personal information from you. We
      do not control and are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of third parties.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="choices">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Your Choices Regarding Your Personal Information</h2>

    <h3>Local-first use</h3>
    <p>
      You can use the App without creating an account with us. You choose which providers to
      install, which projects to open, and whether the App may reach the network for updates or
      agent calls. You can disconnect providers, clear local caches, and delete local workspace
      data from the App or by removing Modesto’s data directory on your machine.
    </p>

    <h3>Cookies and local data</h3>
    <p>
      You can use your browser settings to stop accepting or to delete cookies, although some Site
      features — such as remembering a theme preference — may not function as a result. Information
      stored only on your device remains there until you clear it or uninstall the App.
    </p>

    <h3>Retention and deletion</h3>
    <p>
      We retain communications you send to the project, and operational logs generated by the Site,
      only as long as reasonably necessary to operate the Services, respond to you, protect the
      project from abuse, comply with law, and resolve disputes. We do not retain a cloud copy of
      your local threads or repositories. Deleting the App from your machine does not delete
      information held by a provider you control; contact those providers or delete that
      information directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      To ask us to delete personal information we hold about you — for example an email you sent or
      an issue you want removed from a thread we control — contact us as described below. We may
      need to verify your identity. Public GitHub issues and comments are also subject to GitHub’s
      own retention and deletion tools.
    </p>

    <h3>Your privacy rights</h3>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access to, correction of,
      deletion of, or a portable copy of your personal information, or to restrict or object to
      certain processing. You may also have the right to appeal our response or complain to a
      data-protection authority. We will honor applicable rights after verifying your request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <p class="section-number">06</p>
    <h2>Security of Your Personal Information</h2>
    <p>
      We use administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed for a local-first
      desktop product and a public website. These include encrypted transport for the Site and
      GitHub-hosted updates, minimizing what we collect, using platform-protected storage in the
      App for credentials, and keeping session content on your machine by default.
    </p>
    <p>
      No method of transmission over the Internet or method of electronic storage is completely
      secure. While we use reasonable efforts to protect personal information we hold, we cannot
      guarantee its absolute security. You are responsible for securing the environments,
      coding-agent accounts, credentials, and networks that you connect to Modesto. Our{" "}<a
        href="/security-policy">Security Policy</a
      >{" "}explains how to report a vulnerability and how responsibility is shared.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="international">
    <p class="section-number">07</p>
    <h2>International Users</h2>
    <p>
      The Site and GitHub-hosted release infrastructure are provided from the United States and
      other locations where our providers operate. If you use the Site or the Services from outside
      the United States, your personal information may be transferred to and processed in the
      United States and other countries. Where required, we rely on lawful safeguards for those
      transfers. The App itself processes workspace data on the machine where you install it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <p class="section-number">08</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Site and the Services are not intended for children under 13 years of age, and you must
      be at least 13 years old to use them. We do not knowingly collect, use, or disclose personal
      information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has provided us with
      personal information, please contact us so that we can take appropriate action.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="do-not-track">
    <p class="section-number">09</p>
    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
      We currently do not respond to browser “Do Not Track” signals. Modesto does not use personal
      information for cross-context behavioral or targeted advertising.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="updates">
    <p class="section-number">10</p>
    <h2>Updates to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We reserve the right to update this Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we
      will post the revised Policy at this URL, update the “Last Updated” and “Effective Date”
      above, and provide any additional notice required by law. Except as otherwise indicated,
      changes become effective when the revised Policy is posted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">11</p>
    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Policy or wish to make a privacy or deletion request,
      contact the Modesto maintainer through the public repository:
    </p>
    <address>
      <strong>Modesto</strong><br />
      Tanner Davidson<br />
      <a href="https://github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto">github.com/Syphon1205/Modesto</a>
    </address>
    <p>
      For security issues, use a private GitHub Security Advisory as described in the{" "}<a
        href="/security-policy">Security Policy</a
      >. Do not open a public issue for an unpatched vulnerability.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
